phpBugTracker "2025" DATABASES
==============================

phpBugTracker 2025 has been installed and used (in various degrees, YMMV) with:
  o MySQL 5.5.27                           (Solaris 10, PHP 5.4.7, in production use)
  o MySQL 8.0.30                           (Oracle Linux 10, RHEL10, Remi PHP 8.4.17)
  o PostgreSQL 16.4, 18.1                  (Oracle Linux 10, RHEL10, Remi PHP 8.4.17)
  o SQLite3 3.46.1                         (Oracle Linux 10, Remi PHP 8.4.17)
  o Oracle Cloud Autonomous Database 18c   (Oracle Linux 10, Remi PHP 8.4.7)

phpBugTracker 2025 does not work with MS SQLServer unless you are using PHP 5 and
has not been tested or verified. SQLServer according to the phpBugTracker 1.0.5
information was a valid database backend choice for PHP 5.

The PEAR team officially marked the PEAR::DB MSSQL driver as deprecated since the
driver relies on the legacy ext/mssql PHP 5 extension and this extention has been 
removed in PHP 7. It is no longer supported in modern versions of PHP 7+ and
the PEAR::DB code has not been updated to use the current PHP sqlsvr_* extension.

Quick How To Database Creation :

MySQL
-------------------------------------
mysql> CREATE DATABASE `phpbugtracker` DEFAULT CHARACTER SET utf8mb3 COLLATE utf8_general_ci;
mysql> CREATE USER `bugbuster`@`localhost` IDENTIFIED /* !800 WITH caching_sha2_password */ BY /*'bugbusterpw'*/ 'Raid!32ozSprayCan';
mysql> GRANT CREATE, INDEX, INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE, SELECT ON `phpbugtracker`.* TO `bugbuster`@`localhost`;
mysql> FLUSH PRIVILEGES;
mysql> quit

Test un/pw database connection:
$ mysql -u bugbuster -p phpbugtracker


PostgreSQL 16+
-------------------------------------
root# su - postgres
postgres$ psql
postgres=# CREATE ROLE phpbugtracker_role;
postgres=# GRANT pg_read_all_data  TO phpbugtracker_role;
postgres=# GRANT pg_write_all_data TO phpbugtracker_role;
postgres=# CREATE USER bugbuster WITH LOGIN ENCRYPTED PASSWORD 'bugbusterpw' IN ROLE phpbugtracker_role;
postgres=# CREATE DATABASE phpbugtracker WITH OWNER phpbugtracker_role;
postgres=# \quit

Test un/pw database connection:
postgres$ psql -h localhost -U bugbuster -d phpbugtracker -W
phpbugtracker=> \quit
[postgres@virtnic ~]$  exit
root#


