 SQLite3
-------------------------------------
SQLite3 database will be created at the time of install if the database does not
currently exist and PHP sqlite3 has the OS permissions to do so. It is not necessary 
to create the database beforehand. 

Note that the parent directory containing the sqlite3 database
must be writable to the webserver (and writeable SELinux context allowance when SELinux is present). 
Running the script setperms.sh will do all this for you on the local directory "db".

At browser install time you can specify the full or local path to this location, i.e. "db/phpbugtracker.db"


